# Lisp vocabulary that tools/lisp-candidates.sh reports in new lines, so
# that a Lisp-ism nobody has decided on yet is seen before it lands
# (PORTING.md, "Fortran-first decision guide").  It only warns: a word here
# is a candidate to look at, not an error.  Each candidate a PR adds is
# listed in the PR description with its decision: confirmed by the owner
# (and then a line of tools/fortran-names), or why it is not a Lisp-ism
# here (a keyboard macro, a POSIX signal, a Lisp mode).
#
# fortran-names: off
# One word per line, matched as a whole word in prose and as an
# underscore-delimited part of an identifier, ignoring case.  Words the
# owner has already decided (defun, sexp, alist, nil, ...) are enforced by
# tools/fortran-names and the prose check, and are not repeated here.
# fortran-names: on
